      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2013 American Headache Society.",
        "AbstractText": "Synovial cysts of the temporomandibular joint are rare, and to our knowledge, only 14 cases have been reported. The most common presentation is local pain and swelling. We present a case of a synovial cyst presenting with neuralgia in the distribution of the auriculotemporal nerve, initially misdiagnosed as trigeminal neuralgia."
      },
